# No Type Any - Use Specific Types (BLOCKING)

RULE: Use specific types (TypedDict, Pydantic, Protocol, TypeVar, dict[str, X]). Never use Any — including dict[str, Any]. Check dependency source code to determine actual type. Only audited bypasses in QUALITY_GATE_BYPASS_AUDIT.md may pass.
WHY: Any defeats type checking — no autocomplete, no refactoring safety, runtime errors instead of compile-time. reportAny is BLOCKING in quality gates. dict[str, Any] is NO LONGER EXEMPT.
CODEX: 06-coding-standards/README.md#type-hints

DO:
  def process(data: dict[str, str]) -> str: return data.get("key", "")
  class Config(TypedDict): max_workers: int; venues: list[str]
  Use Protocol for duck typing; TypeVar for generics

TYPED API RESPONSES (MANDATORY):
  When consuming external HTTP/REST APIs (exchanges, data providers, etc.):
  1. Create frozen Pydantic BaseModel classes mirroring the API response schema
  2. Place them in a _<provider>_models.py file next to the adapter
  3. Use model_validate() at the API boundary to parse raw dicts into typed models
  4. Access fields via typed attributes, never .get() chains on raw dicts
  5. For APIs with non-Pythonic keys, use Field(alias="PascalCase") with model_config = {"populate_by_name": True}
  EXEMPLAR: unified-sports-execution-interface/adapters/exchanges/_matchbook_models.py
  CODEX: 06-coding-standards/README.md#type-hints

NEVER:
  def process(data: Any) -> Any:
  config: dict[str, Any] = load_config()
  result = await response.json(); result["key"]  # untyped dict access
  result.get("nested", {}).get("field", "")  # .get() chains on raw API responses
  Relax reportAny; add baseline files
